-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Tranz Am
  Publisher   Ultimate Play The Game, 1983
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch
  (one of these files):

  File        Tranz Am (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)[16K].tzx
  MD5         3fab81f68c6b23fc831df567d43384df

  File        Tranz Am (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)[16K].tap
  MD5         6e8f34425daf27e2c58b948dbe4dd0db

  File        Tranz Am (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)[a][16K].tzx
  MD5         0aa34cabd24c556cabe436a23f7f7e1a

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    All 28 pictures painted with 13 fixed colours: trees, cactus,
              signs, the pump and the cup in their own colours; the cars keep
              the game's body colour (red for yours) with painted wheels and
              trim. A first pass. Off by default. A painted set, colourist not
              named.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.2: Starts with the Next's DivMMC automap switched off:
              NextZXOS leaves it on, and on current cores that could crash the
              game or spoil its drawing

  Note        The cars and the roadside items are hardware sprites in their
              own colours, laid on the pixels the game still draws, so the car
              keeps its colour as it crosses a tree, a rock or a cup and the
              item keeps its own. Enhanced paints them. Proven on machine-
              played games and on every graphic through the game's own draw
              routine; night and the cups are not proven in play. Pace: kept
              by design, the same method as Jet Pac 1.3; not measured for this
              game.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite fuel
   3  Infinite temperature
   4  Immune to cars
   5  Immune to obstacles

  From an archive .pok for this game, each checked against this dump by
  reading the code it changes. Infinite lives also tested in machine play: the
  lives count never falls. The others are not played.

